CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Two threads store to their own element of an array whose size is symbolic,
which field sensitivity cannot split into elements. The store was
`data#new == with(data#old, i, v)` built from the thread's last view of the
whole array and published as a whole, so it put back the element the other
thread had just stored: each thread could read its own element back as 0.
The store now reads the old value and writes the new one in an atomic
section of its own.

Reported FAILED before the fix, SUCCESSFUL after. Reduced from
pthread-lit/sssc12_variant and weaver/popl20-more-vector-add (unreach-call).

See `symbolic_size_store_shared_element` (a real failure, must stay FAILED)
and `symbolic_size_store_shared_element_race`.
